cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Explainable Crop Yield Prediction Using Earth Observation Data"

authors:
  - family-names: Alfeen
    given-names: Ubaidh

version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-01-07
license: Apache-2.0
url: "https://github.com/Alfeenubaidh/crop_prediction_model"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Alfeenubaidh/crop_prediction_model"

abstract: >
  End-to-end machine learning system for regional crop yield prediction
  across 5 Indian states (Punjab, Haryana, Rajasthan, Uttar Pradesh,
  Chandigarh) using satellite-derived NDVI, NASA POWER climate variables,
  soil organic carbon, and historical yield records (2011-2022).
  The system employs a teacher-student distillation architecture
  (Stacking Regressor to LightGBM) with leakage-safe temporal feature
  engineering, conformal prediction intervals, and SHAP-based
  explainability. Served via a FastAPI inference layer and a React
  frontend with Firebase authentication.

keywords:
  - crop yield prediction
  - machine learning
  - remote sensing
  - NDVI
  - LightGBM
  - knowledge distillation
  - SHAP explainability
  - conformal prediction
  - India agriculture
  - Earth observation
